<section class="fragment-design-contract" data-artifact="design-contract" data-component="match-control">

  <h2 class="sdlc-h2">Coverage grid · element × state</h2>
  <p class="dc-lede">Ten elements against the eight states in the contract. A filled cell is a state this contract commits to for that element. An empty cell is a state the element does not have.</p>

  <div class="dc-grid-wrap">
    <table class="dc-grid">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="dc-rowhead">Element</th>
          <th scope="col">default</th>
          <th scope="col">hover</th>
          <th scope="col">focus</th>
          <th scope="col">active</th>
          <th scope="col">disabled</th>
          <th scope="col">loading</th>
          <th scope="col">empty</th>
          <th scope="col">error</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Page grid</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class="is-on" aria-label="loading committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td class="is-on" aria-label="error committed">&#9632;</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Pitch canvas</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class="is-on" aria-label="loading committed">&#9632;</td><td class="is-on" aria-label="empty committed">&#9632;</td><td class="is-on" aria-label="error committed">&#9632;</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Player marker</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Ball and trail</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">match-control button</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td class="is-on" aria-label="hover committed">&#9632;</td><td class="is-on" aria-label="focus committed">&#9632;</td><td class="is-on" aria-label="active committed">&#9632;</td><td class="is-on" aria-label="disabled committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Playback control strip</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class="is-on" aria-label="disabled committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Lag notice</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class="is-on" aria-label="error committed">&#9632;</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Numeric readouts</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Touchline mark</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row" class="dc-rowhead">Token file</th><td class="is-on" aria-label="default committed">&#9632;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="sdlc-h2">The mark is the touchline</h2>
  <p class="dc-lede">The one figure this contract draws rather than describes. Three zones, one marker, one ball, no image file. The same function draws every club crest with kit colours in place of the turf.</p>

  <div class="dc-mark-row">
    <figure class="dc-mark">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" width="120" height="120" role="img" aria-labelledby="dc-mark-primary-t">
        <title id="dc-mark-primary-t">Primary mark: turf tile, white touchline at 58 percent, pitchside band below</title>
        <defs><clipPath id="dc-clip-a"><rect x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120" rx="25.2" ry="25.2"/></clipPath></defs>
        <g clip-path="url(#dc-clip-a)">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120" fill="oklch(0.62 0.13 145)"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="26" r="17" fill="none" stroke="oklch(0.97 0.01 145)" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.55"/>
          <rect x="0" y="67.2" width="120" height="3" fill="oklch(0.97 0.01 145)"/>
          <rect x="0" y="70.2" width="120" height="49.8" fill="oklch(0.28 0.03 250)"/>
          <circle cx="44" cy="48" r="9" fill="oklch(0.55 0.17 250)" stroke="oklch(0.97 0.01 145)" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="74" cy="56" r="4.5" fill="oklch(0.97 0.01 145)"/>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>primary</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="dc-mark">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" width="120" height="120" role="img" aria-labelledby="dc-mark-rev-t">
        <title id="dc-mark-rev-t">Reversed mark: paper tile with a brand touchline</title>
        <defs><clipPath id="dc-clip-b"><rect x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120" rx="25.2" ry="25.2"/></clipPath></defs>
        <g clip-path="url(#dc-clip-b)">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120" fill="oklch(0.985 0.006 250)"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="26" r="17" fill="none" stroke="oklch(0.90 0.008 250)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="0" y="67.2" width="120" height="3" fill="oklch(0.55 0.17 250)"/>
          <rect x="0" y="70.2" width="120" height="49.8" fill="oklch(0.90 0.008 250)"/>
          <circle cx="44" cy="48" r="9" fill="oklch(0.55 0.17 250)" stroke="oklch(0.985 0.006 250)" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="74" cy="56" r="4.5" fill="oklch(0.24 0.02 250)"/>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>reversed</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="dc-mark">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" width="120" height="120" role="img" aria-labelledby="dc-mark-crest-t">
        <title id="dc-mark-crest-t">Club crest: the same function with kit colours in place of the turf</title>
        <defs><clipPath id="dc-clip-c"><rect x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120" rx="25.2" ry="25.2"/></clipPath></defs>
        <g clip-path="url(#dc-clip-c)">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120" fill="oklch(0.52 0.19 22)"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="26" r="17" fill="none" stroke="oklch(0.97 0.01 145)" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.5"/>
          <rect x="0" y="67.2" width="120" height="3" fill="oklch(0.97 0.01 145)"/>
          <rect x="0" y="70.2" width="120" height="49.8" fill="oklch(0.28 0.03 250)"/>
          <circle cx="44" cy="48" r="9" fill="oklch(0.52 0.19 22)" stroke="oklch(0.30 0.02 250)" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="74" cy="56" r="4.5" fill="oklch(0.97 0.01 145)"/>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>club crest</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <p class="dc-note">Corner radius is tile size &times; 0.21, so 120 &times; 0.21 = 25.2. The touchline sits at 58 percent of the tile height. The crest reuses the same three zones with the club's clamped kit primary as the field.</p>

  <h2 class="sdlc-h2">Per-element obligations</h2>
  <p class="dc-lede">Ten rows. Each opens to the tokens it must use, the states it must cover, and the requirement <code>/wf implement</code> builds against.</p>

  <div class="dc-rows">
    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Page grid</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">6 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">3 states</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">CSS Grid at 1280 by 800. Row one is the 56-pixel header; row two holds three fixed columns of 336, 616 and 296 pixels with an 8-pixel gutter. No breakpoints and no fluid tracks, because <code>stack.platforms</code> names one desktop target. <code>viewer-pitch</code> builds the header and both side columns empty so the pitch lands at its shipping position.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-header-h</code> <code>--tl-col-left</code> <code>--tl-col-mid</code> <code>--tl-col-right</code> <code>--tl-gap</code> <code>--tl-bg</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Pitch canvas</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">6 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">4 states</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">Exactly 616 by 411 CSS pixels, with the backing store multiplied by <code>devicePixelRatio</code> and the context scaled to match. Markings are drawn from the engine's own 105 by 68 metre space centred on the origin, so a rendered position maps one to one onto a simulated position. The loading state is a skeleton pitch in <code>--tl-skeleton</code>, never a spinner. <code>role="img"</code> with a label, plus a visually hidden <code>aria-live</code> region mirroring clock, speed and lag in text.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-pitch</code> <code>--tl-pitch-line</code> <code>--tl-pitch-h</code> <code>--tl-col-mid</code> <code>--tl-radius-md</code> <code>--tl-line</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Player marker</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">4 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">1 state</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">A disc filled with the club's safe kit primary; a ring in the safe kit secondary when that colour measures 3:1 against turf, otherwise <code>--tl-pitch-line</code>. The shirt number is white or ink, whichever contrasts more with the fill, drawn at 10 pixels in IBM Plex Sans 600. Every kit hex converts to OKLCH and clamps its lightness into 0.20 to 0.88 before the 3:1 test runs, because <code>content/teams/default-a.json</code> ships pure black.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-pitch</code> <code>--tl-pitch-line</code> <code>--tl-fg</code> <code>--tl-on-brand</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Ball and trail</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">2 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">1 state</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">The ball plus the last N tick positions at falling alpha, drawn as one path rather than N strokes. The trail belongs to the ball alone; no player carries one.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-pitch-line</code> <code>--tl-fg</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">match-control button</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">12 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">5 states</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">Four heights (28, 36, 44, 52) and two themes defined in full, with <code>viewer-pitch</code> shipping the 28 and 36 sizes so later slices add no new geometry. Colour transition at 150 ms on <code>--tl-ease</code>; no press-scale, because the playback strip is pressed tens of times per match and the frequency rule in <code>animate.md</code> removes motion there. A static variant turns the press-scale off. Focus ring at 3:1 via <code>:focus-visible</code>. Any button under 40 by 40 carries a centred pseudo-element hit area, and adjacent hit areas never overlap.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-brand</code> <code>--tl-brand-hover</code> <code>--tl-brand-pressed</code> <code>--tl-on-brand</code> <code>--tl-ring</code> <code>--tl-radius-sm</code> <code>--tl-padx-md</code> <code>--tl-pady-md</code> <code>--tl-gap</code> <code>--tl-font-md</code> <code>--tl-ease</code> <code>--tl-shadow-1</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Playback control strip</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">5 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">2 states</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">A 40-pixel strip immediately under the pitch, holding play and pause, the 1x to 8x speed selector, skip to next stoppage, and the rewind scrubber. Concentric radius: 6 pixels of padding around <code>--tl-radius-sm</code> buttons gives the strip <code>--tl-radius-md</code>. The play triangle shifts 2 pixels right of geometric centre.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-controls-h</code> <code>--tl-panel</code> <code>--tl-radius-md</code> <code>--tl-gap</code> <code>--tl-line</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Lag notice</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">6 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">2 states</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">Names the sustained speed in words and digits, for example "Playing at 3x &mdash; the engine sustains 3x". Colour never carries the state alone. Enter at 200 ms on <code>--tl-ease</code> with opacity and an 8-pixel rise; exit at 150 ms on <code>ease-in</code>. A transition, never a keyframe, so a rapidly re-triggered notice retargets instead of restarting.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-warning</code> <code>--tl-fg</code> <code>--tl-panel</code> <code>--tl-radius-sm</code> <code>--tl-font-num</code> <code>--tl-ease</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Numeric readouts</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">4 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">1 state</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">Clock, speed, frame-time counter and memory gauge all carry <code>font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums</code> so the row does not twitch as values change. Each must measure at least 4.5:1 against <code>--tl-panel</code>, proved before any banner motion is written. This is the brief's named top risk and PRODUCT.md's second strategic principle.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-font-num</code> <code>--tl-fg</code> <code>--tl-panel</code> <code>--tl-fg-muted</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Touchline mark</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">3 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">1 state</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">One exported JavaScript function draws three zones: the field above, a white line at 58 percent of the tile height, and the pitchside band below. Inputs are the tile size and a corner radius of tile size times 0.21. One marker and the ball sit on the field. Four variants: primary, reversed, pitchside, mono. Never loaded from an image file. Club crests call the same function with kit colours in place of the turf.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-pitch</code> <code>--tl-pitch-line</code> <code>--tl-pitchside-bg</code></p></details>

    <details class="dc-row"><summary><span class="dc-el">Token file</span><span class="dc-chips"><span class="dc-chip">7 tokens</span><span class="dc-chip">1 state</span></span></summary>
      <p class="dc-req">One <code>:root</code> block in <code>web/tokens.css</code> is the single source of every colour, radius, spacing, font and easing value. Every value is OKLCH; no pure black and no pure white appears anywhere. The <code>--tl-</code> prefix supersedes the <code>--mv-</code> prefix in <code>02b-design.md</code> and <code>02b-design.yaml</code>, which were written before the product was named. DESIGN.md gains the ten new rows in the same step so the two files never disagree.</p>
      <p class="dc-toks"><code>--tl-bg</code> <code>--tl-fg</code> <code>--tl-brand</code> <code>--tl-pitch</code> <code>--tl-ring</code> <code>--tl-ease</code> <code>--tl-shadow-1</code></p></details>
  </div>

  <h2 class="sdlc-h2">Anti-patterns</h2>

  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Football Manager 3D clutter.</strong> No overlay on the pitch beyond the score bug and the goal banner, and nothing drawn over a player marker.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Sponsor-board clutter.</strong> No logos and no advertising boards on or beside the pitch.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Arcade styling.</strong> No drop shadow, glow, or motion trail on a player marker. The trail belongs to the ball alone.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Purple-blue gradient.</strong> Banned anywhere, including the header band, which stays flat <code>--tl-brand</code>.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Nested cards.</strong> The pitch panel holds the canvas directly and contains no second card.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Decorative side accent stripe.</strong> Use a full hairline or a background tint instead.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Bounce or elastic easing.</strong> Banned, including on the scrubber handle. <code>bounce</code> stays 0.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Pure black or pure white.</strong> Banned, including a kit colour read from a team file. Clamp the lightness first.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>A spinner in a content area.</strong> The pitch shows a skeleton.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>A font service.</strong> Both faces load from <code>web/fonts/</code> as <code>woff2</code>.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>A logo loaded from an image file.</strong> The mark is drawn by <code>web/mark.mjs</code>.</aside>
  <aside class="callout callout-warn dc-anti"><strong>Colour as the only state signal.</strong> The lag notice carries its state in words.</aside>

  <style>
    .fragment-design-contract .dc-lede { color: var(--tl-fg-muted, oklch(0.48 0.02 250)); margin: 0 0 12px; max-width: 70ch; }
    .fragment-design-contract .dc-note { color: var(--tl-fg-muted, oklch(0.48 0.02 250)); font-size: 13px; margin: 8px 0 0; }
    .fragment-design-contract .dc-grid-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .fragment-design-contract .dc-grid { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
